{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "All structural obligations are met.\n\n- **`OutlineLang` implementation.** In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs`, the `language!(PlainText, super::plain::PROFILE, \"plain-text-structural-v1\")` invocation (`macro@e44d6e074366`) expands to `pub struct PlainText` and `impl super::OutlineLang for PlainText`. The impl provides `name`, `extensions`, `outline`, `fingerprint_scheme` and `search_structure`. Those are the methods the `OutlineLang` trait in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#trait[OutlineLang]` declares, with the signatures the `language_provider` requirement lists.\n- **Default value, cheap clone.** The macro derives `Clone, Copy, Debug, Default` on a unit struct. The default value is therefore `Copy`, which makes it cheaply cloneable. It holds no per-instance configuration. The profile is a static.\n- **No claimed extensions.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` sets `extensions: &[]` and `language: None`. `PlainText::extensions()` returns that empty slice.\n- **Constructor selection.**\n  - `OutlineContent::from_source` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs` calls `languages::registry().for_path(filename)`. If that returns nothing, it falls back to `Self::from_source_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`.\n  - `Registry::for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/language.rs` returns `None` through `path.extension()?` for filenames with no extension. It also returns `None` when no provider claims the lowercased extension.\n  - `from_path` delegates to `from_source`, so both filename-based constructors get the fallback.\n\nTests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs` cover this and carry `{test}` markers: `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors`, `bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline` (asserts the name is `plain-text` and the extensions are empty) and `plain_line_fingerprints_use_sha256_words_without_losing_boundaries`.\n\nThe review found no gaps, ambiguities or acknowledgments.",
  "references": "d364693a64f673cea5b31c5d57cc4436a3d085824fd398288e275ce0c804733a",
